      "message": "[error] Line 389: 🔴 `handleRouteChange()` disposes the current `ioUnit_` before attempting re-init, and on failure it calls `destroyAudioLayer()`, which disposes `ioUnit_` again unconditionally. If `initAudioLayerIO(stream)` fails, this is a second dispose on an invalid/stale `AudioUnit` handle and can lead to undefined behavior/crash. Make disposal idempotent: guard `disposeAudioUnit()` with `if (ioUnit_)`, reset `ioUnit_ \u003d nullptr` after dispose, and avoid the second dispose path when re-init failed before a new unit was created (or split teardown for session deactivation vs unit disposal).",
